     '[{"label": "A", "text": "The recipe for making any creature is written in its DNA. So last November when geneticists published the near-complete DNA sequence of the long-extinct woolly mammoth, there was much speculation about whether we could bring this behemoth back to life. Creating a living, breathing creature from a genome sequence that exists only in a computer''s memory is not possible right now. But someone someday is sure to try it, ________ Stephan Schuster, a _________ biologist at Pennsylvania State University, University Park, and a _________ force behind the mammoth genome project."}]'::jsonb, 0, 'medium', 'Academic Reading',
