    ('rp-pte-em-rwfib-123', 'pte-2026-01', 'The Food Standards Authority', 'PTE Exam Memories',
     '[{"label": "A", "text": "The Food Standards Authority has ___________ a public warning about the risks of a compound called acrylamide that ____________ in some foods cooked at high temperatures. This means that people should avoid ____________ their roast potatoes, reject thin-crust pizzas and only easily toast their bread. But where is the evidence to support such __________ advice? While studies have shown that acrylamide can cause neurological damage in mice, there is no _______________ evidence that it causes cancer in humans."}]'::jsonb, 0, 'medium', 'Academic Reading',
