    ('pte-em-rwfib-001', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'A Giant Turtle Made', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'A giant turtle made from discarded plastic trash will greet visitors to the British Science Festival this week. The plastic containers, bottles and cups were collected locally in Hull, where the event is taking place at the city'' s university. Standing 3.5m tall (11.5ft), the art installation [[b1]] commissioned by the University of Hull with the aim of raising awareness of plastic waste. Professor Dan Parsons, director of the university'' s Energy and Environment Institute, said: ''Marine pollution is a mounting global challenge, which is [[b2]] having devastating consequences. We have a duty to protect these fragile environments and the marine life and ecosystems which we [[b3]] home. The university has commissioned this installation as a physical [[b4]] of what is ending up in the oceans, but also to ask visitors to campus to stop and think what they could do to try to reduce their own waste.''', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["has", "being", "have", "was"], "correctAnswer": "was"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["only", "already", "otherwise", "yet"], "correctAnswer": "already"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["settle", "call", "originate", "go"], "correctAnswer": "call"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["reminder", "receipt", "reinforcement", "recognition"], "correctAnswer": "reminder"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 4, 'medium',
     ARRAY['PTE', 'Exam Memories', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks']::text[], 'rp-pte-em-rwfib-001', 'g-pte-em-rwfib-001', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('pte-em-rwfib-002', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'It Is Tempting To', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'It is tempting to try to prove that good looks win votes, and many academics have tried. The [[b1]] is that beauty is in the eye of the [[b2]], and you cannot behold a politician''s face without a veil of extraneous prejudice getting in the way. Does George Bush possess a disarming grin, or a facetious [[b3]]? It''s hard to find anyone who can look at the president without assessing him politically as well as [[b4]].', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["struggle", "idea", "difficulty", "controversy"], "correctAnswer": "difficulty"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["lover", "beholder", "builder", "perceiver"], "correctAnswer": "beholder"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["smell", "smear", "smirk", "smirch"], "correctAnswer": "smirk"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["culturally", "physically", "economically", "individually"], "correctAnswer": "physically"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 4, 'medium',
     ARRAY['PTE', 'Exam Memories', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks']::text[], 'rp-pte-em-rwfib-002', 'g-pte-em-rwfib-002', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('pte-em-rwfib-003', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Stress That Tense Feeling', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Stress that tense feeling often connected to having too much to do, too many [[b1]] to pay and not enough time or money - is a common emotion that knows [[b2]] borders. About three-fourths of people in the United States, Australia, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, South Korea and Britain reported experiencing stress on a daily basis, according to AP-Ipsos [[b3]]. Anxious feelings were more intense during the holidays. Germans feel stress more [[b4]] than those in other countries polled. People in the United States [[b5]] financial pressures as the top worry. About half the people polled in Britain said they frequently or sometimes felt that life was beyond their control, the highest level in the 10 countries surveyed.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["practices", "bills", "money", "time"], "correctAnswer": "bills"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["printed", "solid", "dash", "few"], "correctAnswer": "few"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["series", "news", "polling", "pants"], "correctAnswer": "polling"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["intensely", "openly", "early", "traditionally"], "correctAnswer": "intensely"}, {"id": "b5", "options": ["enjoyed", "cited", "created", "exited"], "correctAnswer": "cited"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 5, 'medium',
     ARRAY['PTE', 'Exam Memories', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks']::text[], 'rp-pte-em-rwfib-003', 'g-pte-em-rwfib-003', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('pte-em-rwfib-004', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Our Analysis Of The', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Our analysis of the genetic structure of northern spotted owls across most of the range of the subspecies allowed us to test for genetic discontinuities and identify landscape features that influence the subspecies'' genetic structure. Although no [[b1]] genetic breaks were found in northern spotted owls, [[b2]] landscape features were important in structuring genetic variation. Dry, low elevation valleys and the high elevation Cascade and Olympic Mountains restricted gene flow, while the lower Oregon Coast Range [[b3]] gene flow, acting as a '' genetic corridor.'' The Columbia River did not act as a barrier, [[b4]] owls readily fly over this large river. Thus, even in taxa such as northern spotted owls with potential for long-distance dispersal, landscape features can have an important impact on gene flow and genetic structure.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["distinct", "distinguished", "different", "divergent"], "correctAnswer": "distinct"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["specific", "several", "separate", "a little"], "correctAnswer": "several"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["protected", "prevented", "impeded", "facilitated"], "correctAnswer": "facilitated"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["arguing", "suggesting", "insisting", "sticking"], "correctAnswer": "suggesting"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 4, 'medium',
     ARRAY['PTE', 'Exam Memories', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks']::text[], 'rp-pte-em-rwfib-004', 'g-pte-em-rwfib-004', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('pte-em-rwfib-005', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Want To Know What', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Want to know what will make you happy? Then ask a total stranger - or so says a new study from Harvard University, which shows that another person''s experience is often more [[b1]] than your own best guess.The study, which appears in the current issue of Science, was led by Daniel Gilbert, professor of psychology at Harvard and author of the 2007 bestseller "Stumbling on Happiness," along with Matthew Killingworth and Rebecca Eyre, also of Harvard, and Timothy Wilson of the University of Virginia. "If you want to know how much you will enjoy an experience, you are better off knowing how much someone else enjoyed it than knowing anything about the experience itself," says Gilbert. "Rather than closing our eyes and [[b2]] the future, we should examine the experience of those who have been there. Previous research in psychology, neuroscience, and behavioral economics has shown that people have difficulty predicting what they will like and how much they will like it, which [[b3]] them to make a wide variety of poor decisions. Interventions aimed at [[b4]] the accuracy with which people imagine future events have been generally unsuccessful.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["positive", "predictable", "informal", "informative"], "correctAnswer": "informative"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["imitating", "predicting", "visualizing", "imagining"], "correctAnswer": "imagining"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["leads", "compels", "requires", "forces"], "correctAnswer": "leads"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["reducing", "improving", "enhancing", "controlling"], "correctAnswer": "improving"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 4, 'medium',
     ARRAY['PTE', 'Exam Memories', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks']::text[], 'rp-pte-em-rwfib-005', 'g-pte-em-rwfib-005', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('pte-em-rwfib-006', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Nature Is No Longer', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Nature is no longer an alien [[b1]], but [[b2]] something immediately beautiful, an exuberant [[b3]] with space for us to join in. Bird melodies have always been called songs for a reason. As long as we have been listening, people have [[b4]] there is music coming out of those scissoring beaks.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["enigma", "alien", "mystery", "alienate"], "correctAnswer": "enigma"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["however", "moreover", "additionally", "instead"], "correctAnswer": "instead"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["composition", "product", "opus", "effort"], "correctAnswer": "opus"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["assumed", "presumed", "considered", "consume"], "correctAnswer": "presumed"}]'::jsonb,
     'Select the most grammatically and contextually appropriate word for each blank.', 4, 'medium',
