     'Dictatorship Is Not A', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Dictatorship is not a modern concept. Two thousand years ago, during the period of the Roman Republic, exceptional powers were sometimes given by the Senate to [[b1]] dictators such as Sulla and Julius Caesar. The [[b2]] was that the dictatorship would be temporary and that it would make it possible to take swift and effective action to deal with an emergency. There is some [[b3]] as to how the term should be applied today. Should it be used in its original form to describe the temporary exercise of emergency powers? Or can it now be [[b4]] in a much broader sense - as common usage suggests?', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["special", "individual", "group", "others"], "correctAnswer": "individual"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["intention", "intent", "international", "sample"], "correctAnswer": "intention"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["agreement", "moment", "treatment", "treatment", "disagreement"], "correctAnswer": "disagreement"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["replied", "applied", "agree", "regretted"], "correctAnswer": "applied"}]'::jsonb,
