     'An Economist Sees The', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'An economist sees the world basically through a typical micro-economic [[b1]]. That involves things like thinking at the margin, rationality, opportunity cost, trade-offs. Economists like any other [[b2]], or dogma has its own jargon and its own rules, and its own way of seeing the world. So basically economics, or economists in general tend to apply micro-economic [[b3]] like that to explain the way humans behave and to make [[b4]] about the future.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["toolkit", "concern", "rate", "power"], "correctAnswer": "toolkit"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["degree", "title", "tuition", "discipline"], "correctAnswer": "discipline"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["funds", "concepts", "tariffs", "scales"], "correctAnswer": "concepts"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["preferences", "predictions", "reviews", "regrets"], "correctAnswer": "predictions"}]'::jsonb,
