     'An Analysis Of More', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'An analysis of more than 500 graduates found no significant difference between business schools that offered traditional courses and those that emphasise a ''learning-by-doing'' approach to entrepreneurship education. The research challenges the ongoing trend across higher education institutes (HEIs) of [[b1]] on experiential learning, and suggests that universities need to reconsider their approach if they [[b2]] increase entrepreneurship among their students. Ms Inna Kozlinska, research associate at Aston Business School and author of the study, said: ''Entrepreneurship education [[b3]] as a major force capable of generating long-term socio-economic changes through developing entrepreneurial, creative, flexible and wise individuals. There is an ongoing shift towards experiential learning in business schools, [[b4]] there is little empirical evidence to suggest this approach has better impact than traditional learning.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["acclaiming", "turning", "spreading", "focusing"], "correctAnswer": "focusing"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["are", "are to", "going to", "to"], "correctAnswer": "are to"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["is seen", "has seen", "sees", "is seeing", "is seem"], "correctAnswer": "is seem"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["yet", "unless", "besides", "so"], "correctAnswer": "yet"}]'::jsonb,
