     'San Francisco''S Golden Gate', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'San Francisco''s Golden Gate Bridge, a stunning technological and artistic achievement, [[b1]] to the public after five years of construction. On opening day-"Pedestrian Day"- some 200,000 bridge walkers [[b2]] at the 4,200-foot-long suspension bridge, which spans the Golden Gate Strait at the entrance to San Francisco Bay and [[b3]] San Francisco and Marin County. On May 28, the Golden Gate Bridge opened to [[b4]] traffic. On May 27, 1937, the Golden Gate Bridge was opened to great acclaim, a [[b5]] of progress in the Bay Area during a time of economic crisis. At 4,200 feet, it was the longest bridge in the world [[b6]] the completion of New York City''s Verrazano-Narrows Bridge in 1964. Today, the Golden Gate Bridge remains one of the world''s most recognizable architectural structures.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["opens", "closes", "appears", "equals"], "correctAnswer": "opens"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["stationed", "looked", "marveled", "laughed"], "correctAnswer": "marveled"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["separates", "connects", "channels", "differentiates"], "correctAnswer": "connects"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["aquatic", "vehicular", "airborne", "watertight"], "correctAnswer": "vehicular"}, {"id": "b5", "options": ["denial", "symbol", "technique", "yield"], "correctAnswer": "symbol"}, {"id": "b6", "options": ["since", "until", "along", "within"], "correctAnswer": "until"}]'::jsonb,
