     'Some People Who Are', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Some people who are bitten by snakes (or suspect or imagine that they have been bitten) may develop quite striking symptoms and signs, even when no venom has been [[b1]]. This results from an understandable fear of the consequences of a real venomous bite. Anxious people may hyperventilate so that they develop pins-and-needles [[b2]] in the extremities, spasm of their hands and feet, and dizziness. Some may develop vasovagal shock after the bite or suspected bite, with faintness and collapse with profound slowing of the heart. Others may become highly agitated and [[b3]] and may manifest a wide range of misleading symptoms. The clinical [[b4]] of a snakebite victim varies with the age and size of the patient, the species of snake, the number and location of the bites, and the quantity and toxicity of the venom.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["proven", "eaten", "injected", "taken"], "correctAnswer": "injected"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["sensation", "provision", "promotion", "emotion"], "correctAnswer": "sensation"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["calm", "composed", "rational", "irrational"], "correctAnswer": "irrational"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["perception", "presentation", "view", "valuation"], "correctAnswer": "presentation"}]'::jsonb,
