     'In Silicon Valley, To', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'In Silicon Valley, to make a device "smart" means to add internet [[b1]], allowing it to collect, send, and receive data, often while learning and [[b2]] to user preferences. The technology industry has invested wholesale in the idea that "smart" means better, so we have smartphones. Soon enough, we''ll have a smart city: Sidewalk Labs. It is not the first smart city municipalities around the world have [[b3]] smart infrastructure like artificial-intelligence-enabled traffic lights, but it might be the most [[b4]]. The project''s 200-page wish list of features is astounding. The "vision document" imagines not only the revitalization of a 12-acre plot that has sat largely vacant since its heyday as an industrial port, but its transformation into a micro-city [[b5]] with smart technologies that will use data to disrupt everything from traffic congestion to health care, housing, zoning regulations, and greenhouse-gas emissions.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["detachment", "disjunction", "connectivity", "connect"], "correctAnswer": "connectivity"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["teaching", "adapting", "watching", "seeing"], "correctAnswer": "adapting"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["renounce", "return adopted", "requdiate", "adopted"], "correctAnswer": "adopted"}, {"id": "b4", "options": ["unenthusiastic", "facile", "satisfied", "ambitious"], "correctAnswer": "ambitious"}, {"id": "b5", "options": ["unfurnished", "outfitted", "unequipped", "bared", "a outfitted"], "correctAnswer": "a outfitted"}]'::jsonb,
