     'The trigger point causes the rest of the fiber segments to be [[b1]] to capacity. It becomes a tight band. Normally the regular contracting and releasing of these little segments circulates blood in the capillaries that supply them (the segments) with their nutrients. When they hold this [[b2]], blood flow is stopped to that area, there is not an oxygen supply, and waste products are not [[b3]] out. The trigger point then sends out pain signals until the trigger point is put in a position of rest again.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "extended"}, {"id": "B", "text": "stretched"}, {"id": "C", "text": "pushed"}, {"id": "D", "text": "contraction"}, {"id": "E", "text": "taken"}, {"id": "F", "text": "release"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["extended", "stretched", "pushed", "contraction", "taken", "release"], "correctAnswer": "stretched"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["extended", "stretched", "pushed", "contraction", "taken", "release"], "correctAnswer": "contraction"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["extended", "stretched", "pushed", "contraction", "taken", "release"], "correctAnswer": "pushed"}]'::jsonb,
