     'The Precise Relationship Between', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The precise relationship between fiction and life been debated extensively. Most modem critics agree that, whatever its apparent factual content or verisimilitude, fiction is finally to e regarded as a structured imitation of life and should not be confused with literal [[b1]] of life itself. While fiction is a work of the imagination rather than [[b2]], it can also be based closely on real events, sometimes experienced by the author. In a work of fiction, the author not the same [[b3]] the narrator, the voice that tells the story. Authors maintain a distance from their characters. Sometimes that distance is obvious for instance, if a male writer tells a story from the point of view of a female character. Other times it is not so obvious, especially if we know something of the author''s life and there are clear connections between the story and the author''s life. The writer of fiction is free to choose his or her subject matter and if free to invent, select, and [[b4]] fictional elements to [[b5]] his or her purpose. The elements of fiction are the different components that up a work of fiction. All literature explores a theme or significant truth expressed in various elements such as character, plot, setting, point of view, style, and toe that are essential and specific to each work of fiction. All of these elements bind a literary work into a consistent whole and give it unity. Understanding these elements can help.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Move"}, {"id": "B", "text": "reality"}, {"id": "C", "text": "arrange"}, {"id": "D", "text": "for"}, {"id": "E", "text": "transcription"}, {"id": "F", "text": "achieve"}, {"id": "G", "text": "rationality"}, {"id": "H", "text": "as complete"}, {"id": "I", "text": "as"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["Move", "reality", "arrange", "for", "transcription", "achieve", "rationality", "as complete", "as"], "correctAnswer": "transcription"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["Move", "reality", "arrange", "for", "transcri