    ('pte-em-rfib-189', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Electric Eels Are Born', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Electric eels are born to shock. Thanks to cells called electrocytes which, stacked like batteries, make up 80% of their bodies, these cunning South American [[b1]] can deliver debilitating blows of up to 600 volts to their prey. But they''ve harnessed their electricity to pack even bigger punches. Last year, Vanderbilt University biologist Kenneth Catania revealed electric eels bring their positively charged head and negatively charged [[b2]] closer together to generate a more powerful [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "objects"}, {"id": "B", "text": "current"}, {"id": "C", "text": "limb"}, {"id": "D", "text": "hunters"}, {"id": "E", "text": "tail"}, {"id": "F", "text": "engine"}, {"id": "G", "text": "hunter"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["objects", "current", "limb", "hunters", "tail", "engine", "hunter"], "correctAnswer": "hunter"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["objects", "current", "limb", "hunters", "tail", "engine", "hunter"], "correctAnswer": "tail"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["objects", "current", "limb", "hunters", "tail", "engine", "hunter"], "correctAnswer": "current"}]'::jsonb,
